</div>
  <p>If <b>face</b> is <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/ALL_SIDES" target="_blank">ALL_SIDES</a> then the function works on all sides.</p>
  <h2><a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlSetColor/Newbie_Notes" target="_blank">Newbie Notes</a></h2>
  <p>llSetColor changes the color of a prim, either on a specific side (face) or the entire prim.</p>
  <p>Example:</p>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll.SetColor(vector(r, g, b), ALL_SIDES)`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`llSetColor(<r, g, b>, ALL_SIDES);`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <p><b>r, g, b</b>: values for red, green, blue ranging from &lt;0.0, 0.0, 0.0&gt; (black) to &lt;1.0, 1.0, 1.0&gt; (white)</p>
  <p>To continue reading see: <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlSetColor/Newbie_Notes" target="_blank">Newbie Notes</a></p>
  <h2>Caveats</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The function silently fails if its <b>face</b> value indicates a face that does not exist.</li>
    <li><p>llSetColor will have no visible effect on faces with a PBR material. To work on faces both with and without a PBR material, use this snippet:</p>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll = llcompat



if ll.IsLinkGLTFMaterial(LINK_THIS, ALL_SIDES) ~= 0 then
    ll.SetLinkGLTFOverrides(LINK_THIS, ALL_SIDES, {OVERRIDE_GLTF_BASE_COLOR_FACTOR, ll.sRGB2Linear(color)})
else
    ll.SetColor(color, ALL_SIDES)
end
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`
if (llIsLinkGLTFMaterial(LINK_THIS, ALL_SIDES)) {
    llSetLinkGLTFOverrides(LINK_THIS, ALL_SIDES, [OVERRIDE_GLTF_BASE_COLOR_FACTOR, llsRGB2Linear(color)]);
} else {
    llSetColor(color, ALL_SIDES);
}
`} lang="lsl" /></div>

</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Examples</h2>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`local face = -1
local color = vector(1.0, 1.0, 1.0)

function LLEvents.touch_start(events)
    local num = #events
    if bit32.bnot(face) ~= 0 then  --quick & dirty but efficient way of testing if face is not equal to -1
        ll.SetColor(color, face)  --restore the color
    end
    face = (face + 1) % ll.GetNumberOfSides()  --increment and keep the face number in range
    color = ll.GetColor(face)  --save the face's color
    ll.SetColor(vector(0.5, 0.0, 0.0), face)  --change the face's color
end
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`integer face = -1;
vector color = <1.0, 1.0, 1.0>;

default
{
    touch_start(integer num)
    {
        if(~face)       //quick & dirty but efficient way of testing if face is not equal to -1
            llSetColor(color, face); //restore the color
        face = (face + 1) % llGetNumberOfSides(); //increment and keep the face number in range
        color = llGetColor(face); //save the face's color
        llSetColor(<0.5, 0.0, 0.0>, face );  //change the face's color
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
